<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  DrillTurret_ShootingJob.xml                Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-21
  ============================================================================

  DRILLTURRET_IS_A_SHOOTING_JOB_1. One field of somebody else's mod, and nothing
  more.

  WHY
  ===
  The campaign's Jawa carry a gene with `disabledWorkTags: Mining` — they do not
  dig. The drill turret is how they mine anyway: by machine, not by hand. But
  `OperateDrillTurret` ships with `workType Mining`, so that same gene would bar
  a Jawa from operating the turret as well as from swinging a pick, which
  defeats the entire point of having one.

  OWNER, 2026-08-21: "I still like shooting for the laser, please make it so."

  WHY `Hunting` IS WHAT "SHOOTING" MEANS HERE
  ===========================================
  Measured across every Core/DLC WorkTypeDef against OFFICIAL-2026-08-21T22-44-59Z.
  Exactly one carries the Shooting skill:

      Hunting    relevantSkills ['Shooting','Animals']
                 workTags Violent, Hunting, Shooting, ManualSkilled, Commoner, AllWork
      Crafting   relevantSkills ['Crafting']
                 workTags ManualSkilled, Commoner, Crafting, AllWork

  ⚠️ THE COST, ACCEPTED WITH THE RULING RATHER THAN DISCOVERED LATER. `Hunting`
  carries `Violent`, so a pawn incapable of violence cannot operate the turret,
  and the job sits in the Hunting work column beside hunting animals. The owner
  was shown this and chose shooting anyway. `Crafting` was the alternative and
  is NOT what was ruled — do not "fix" this to Crafting.

  ⛔ NOTHING ELSE OF DrillTurret's IS TOUCHED, and vanilla's own `Drill`
  WorkGiver is not patched. Re-typing that would change the job for every
  faction in the game. A Jawa being unable to run a deep drill is the ruling
  working, not a gap to close later.

  ⚠️ `PatchOperationFindMod` GUARDS THIS, and it is not decoration. A
  `PatchOperationReplace` whose xpath matches nothing LOGS NOTHING — with the
  DrillTurret mod absent this would fail silently and forever. The guard turns
  that into a clean no-op instead.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>MiningCo. DrillTurret (Continued)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>Defs/WorkGiverDef[defName="OperateDrillTurret"]/workType</xpath>
      <value>
        <workType>Hunting</workType>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
